 Transit Student Organizations Athletics Blue Devil Bands Greek Life Student Veterans Group Student Government Blue Devil Motorsports Student Support Career Services Clinical Counseling Office of International Programs One Stop Center Student Access and Accommodations Student Accounts LGBT Resource Center ABOUT Contact Us Campus Map Directions Facilities Consumer Information Office of the President Marketing Job Openings Faculty and Staff Resources Employee Handbooks Faculty and Staff Directory Organizational Chart Staff Senate Human Resources 25Live Title IX Community Programs Facility Rental High School Summer Programs Marburger STEM Center Robofest History NEWS CALENDAR ALUMNI GIVING FACULTY + STAFF BANNERWEB EHELP Search College of Arts + Sciences Faculty + Staff Home » College of Arts + Sciences » Faculty + Staff Fostering Excellence Through Collaboration The College of Arts and Sciences faculty are passionate scholars and mentors who bring expertise and dedication to every classroom. With a strong emphasis on course-based research experiences, they engage students in hands-on learning that deepens critical thinking and problem-solving skills. Administration + Staff Faculty Adjunct Faculty Faculty Emeritus Marilyn Rands Professor Emerita Natural Sciences mrands@ltu.edu Walter Dean Professor Emeritus of Chemistry Natural Sciences wdean@ltu.edu Richard Marburger Senior Arts + Sciences Advisor Senior Engineering Advisor President Emeritus rem1@ltu.edu Maria Vaz Professor Emerita Natural Sciences mvaz@ltu.edu College of Arts + Sciences Programs Research Course-Based Research Experience Initiatives Core Curriculum Student Success + Services Seminars + Lectures Policies and Procedures AI Resource Hub Departments Humanities, Social Sciences, + Communication In Humanities, Social Sciences, and Communication, we explore what makes us uniquely human. Through ancient and modern texts, social norms, and communication, we uncover how these fields are essential to all careers and human endeavors. Learn more Math + Computer Science In a world of programming, proofs, and unending figures and unfeeling facts, is there room for a touch of magic? Data drives discovery, innovation redefines intelligence, and when curiosity meets logic, mathematics can be miraculous. Learn more Natural Sciences Curiosity drives discovery in biology, chemistry, and physics, guiding us from molecular interactions to chemical reactions and the fundamental laws of nature. Explore what makes you curious. Learn more 1 800 225 5588 21000 West Ten Mile Road Southfield, MI, 48075-1058 Instagram Streamline Icon: https://streamlinehq.com Facebook-f X-twitter Tiktok Linkedin Streamline Icon: https://streamlinehq.com Quick Links News Calendar Alumni Giving Faculty + Staff BannerWeb eHelp Library News Calendar Alumni Giving Faculty + Staff BannerWeb eHelp Library Admissions Apply Explore + Visit Academics Programs Course Catalog Financial Aid Tuition and Fees Apply Explore + Visit Academics Programs Course Catalog Financial Aid Tuition and Fees Student Life Housing Student Support Student Organizations Athletics Bookstore Library Housing Student Support Student Organizations Athletics Bookstore Library About Contact Us Campus Map Job Openings Research + Economic Development Office of the President Office of the Provost Marketing Privacy Policy Contact Us Campus Map Job Openings Research + Economic Development Office of the President Office of the Provost Marketing Privacy Policy ©2026 Lawrence Technological University. All Rights Reserved. Title IX Sitemap Title IX Sitemap"
