nt Veterans Group Student Government Blue Devil Motorsports Student Support Career Services Clinical Counseling Office of International Programs One Stop Center Student Access and Accommodations Student Accounts LGBT Resource Center ABOUT Contact Us Campus Map Directions Facilities Consumer Information Office of the President Marketing Job Openings Faculty and Staff Resources Employee Handbooks Faculty and Staff Directory Organizational Chart Staff Senate Human Resources 25Live Title IX Community Programs Facility Rental High School Summer Programs Marburger STEM Center Robofest History NEWS CALENDAR ALUMNI GIVING FACULTY + STAFF BANNERWEB EHELP Search Career Services Co-Ops Home » Student Life » Student Support » Career Services » Co-Ops Education That Pays off Before Graduation While most colleges offer a diploma, Lawrence Technological University provides the professional experience employers actually demand. Through our co-op program, you can build a high-impact resume and master industry skills in real-time, ensuring you are career-ready the moment you graduate. Experience and education happen side-by-side. At LTU, you can engage in co-op opportunities without stepping away from your classes. LTU’s co-op opportunities connect classroom learning with Michigan’s leading industries—including engineering, manufacturing, technology, construction, architecture and healthcare—so you can build your resume, apply what you learn immediately and graduate with more than a degree: real industry experience. Enrolling in the Co-Op Program can help you gain clarity regarding your career path and selected major! To begin the co-op registration process, email the office at ltuocs@ltu.edu . How Can the Office of Career Services Help You? The Office of Career Services hosts four career fairs on-campus each academic school year. Workshops, career events, and individual career coaching is available to assist you with your career planning process. Handshake is available for your use where you can research employers and apply for co-op positions. Career Services Resources Academic Credit Being a part of the Co-op Program is not a requirement in fulfillment to graduate from Lawrence Tech, but is highly recommended. However, there are academic programs that mandate to complete a co-op, internship, or some type of field experience to graduate. Students should meet with their faculty advisor to discuss the process if that requirement relates to their major(s). Once a student has been offered a co-op position and would like to receive academic credit, then the Office of Career Services will evaluate the work assignment(s) and approve registration. Newly hired co-op students will need to provide the Office of Career Services a copy of the job offer letter and list of job duties to validate co-op employment. Co-op students must have completed a minimum of 55 credits and earned an overall GPA of 2.5 to be in the program. Co-Op Assignments It is important to note that course requirements are based on which co-op practicum a student is enrolled in for each work term. Thus, students in Co-op Practicum I have different requirements than students enrolled in Co-op Practicum II and III. Co-op Practicum III with consist of a formal presentation to be completed in front of peers, Career Services staff, and faculty members. All Co-Op assignments are completed through Canvas. Please login to your Canvas account and select your appropriate Co-Op course. Contact the Office of Career Services at ltuocs@ltu.edu if you have any questions. Contact Us 248.204.3140 ltuocs@ltu.edu Location Taubman Student Services Center, C404 21000 West Ten Mile Road Southfield, MI 48075-1058 Campus Map Hours Monday – Friday 8:00 a.m. – 4:30 p.m. Students: Please schedule an appointment using Handshake for a day and time that works best with your schedule. Staff 1 800 225 5588 21000 West Ten Mile Road Southfield, MI, 48075-1058 Instagram Streamline Icon: https://streamlinehq.com Facebook-f X-twitter Tiktok Linkedin Streamline Icon: https://streamlinehq.com Quick Links News Calendar Alumni Giving Faculty + Staff BannerWeb eHelp Library News Calendar Alumni Giving Faculty + Staff BannerWeb eHelp Library Admissions Apply Explore + Visit Academics Programs Course Catalog Financial Aid Tuition and Fees Apply Explore + Visit Academics Programs Course Catalog Financial Aid Tuition and Fees Student Life Housing Student Support Student Organizations Athletics Bookstore Library Housing Student Support Student Organizations Athletics Bookstore Library About Contact Us Campus Map Job Openings Research + Economic Development Office of the President Office of the Provost Marketing Privacy Policy Contact Us Campus Map Job Openings Research + Economic Development Office of the President Office of the Provost Marketing Privacy Policy ©2026 Lawrence Technological University. All Rights Reserved. Title IX Sitemap Title IX Sitemap"
