nt Organizations Athletics Blue Devil Bands Greek Life Student Veterans Group Student Government Blue Devil Motorsports Student Support Career Services Clinical Counseling Office of International Programs One Stop Center Student Access and Accommodations Student Accounts LGBT Resource Center ABOUT Contact Us Campus Map Directions Facilities Consumer Information Office of the President Marketing Job Openings Faculty and Staff Resources Employee Handbooks Faculty and Staff Directory Organizational Chart Staff Senate Human Resources 25Live Title IX Community Programs Facility Rental High School Summer Programs Marburger STEM Center Robofest History NEWS CALENDAR ALUMNI GIVING FACULTY + STAFF BANNERWEB EHELP Search Job Openings Home » About » Human Resources » Job Openings Thank you for your interest in employment at Lawrence Technological University! Lawrence Technological University (LTU) conducts pre-employment screening on initial candidates for all positions, including a criminal background check, verification of academic credentials, license, certifications, or proof of work history. Lawrence Tech offers a competitive salary and comprehensive benefits package including medical, dental, vision and life insurance; a retirement plan with employer contributions; a vacation and time off policy; a tuition waiver program and much more. While exploring our job openings, we recommend you check out the Benefits Home Page for a listing of the benefits we offer. » Vacant Positions Employment Type... Administrator Faculty Staff Part-Time Browse by Office Admissions Assessment Committee Athletics Bookstore Business Services Campus Dining Campus Facilities Campus Safety Career Services Center for Teaching and Learning Advisory Board Centrepolis Accelerator Clinical Counseling Dean's Council eLearning Finance and Administration Financial Aid Giving Graduate Council Help Desk Services Human Resources Institutional Animal Care and Use Committee Institutional Research Institutional Review Board International Programs IT Service Delivery K-12 Partnerships and Outreach Library Mail Services Marburger STEM Center Marketing and Public Affairs Philanthropy and Alumni Engagement President Emeriti President's Office Provost Council Provost's Office Registrar's Office Research and Economic Development Sponsored Research and Institutional Grants Staff Senate Student Access and Accommodation Student Affairs Technology and Instructional Innovation University Housing University Leadership University Research and Scholarship Council Browse by College Architecture and Design Arts and Sciences Business and IT Engineering Health Sciences Professional and Workforce Development Specs@LTU Study Abroad Browse by Academic Department Allied Health Sciences Architecture Arts Biomedical Engineering Cardiovascular Perfusion Civil and Architectural Engineering Design Doctorate of Health Sciences Electrical and Computer Engineering Engineering Technology Health Sciences Healthcare Administration Humanities Social Sciences and Communication Intraoperative Neuromonitoring Math and Computer Science Mechanical Robotics and Industrial Engineering Natural Sciences Nursing Physician Assistant Studies Job Title Employment Type College or Administrative Office Date Posted Assistant Football Coach Full-Time Athletics July 29, 2026 Clinical Education Assistant for PA Program Full-Time Health Sciences June 23, 2026 Vice President for Finance and Administration & Chief Financial Officer Full-Time Business Services April 7, 2026 Contact Us 248.204.2150 Confidential Fax: 248.204.2118 hr@ltu.edu The Office of Human Resources is located in the Enterprise Center, Suite 210 . Note: The office is located on the 2nd floor of the back building; address 21415 Civic Center Drive. » Notice of Non-Discrimination Policy Lawrence Tech adheres and conforms to all applicable federal, state and local civil rights regulations, statutes and ordinances. No person, student, faculty or staff member will knowingly be discriminated against relative to the above statutes. Lawrence Tech is an Equal Opportunity Employer. » Notice of Disability Services In compliance with Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973 and the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA), those applicants requiring reasonable accommodation to the application and/or interview process should notify the Office of Human Resources for assistance. » E-Verify Notice Lawrence Tech complies with the United States Department of Homeland Security (U.S.Citizenship and Immigration Services) to verify the employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. The university will provide Social Security Administration (SSA) and, if necessary, the Department of Homeland Security (DHS), with information from each new employee’s Form I-9 to confirm work authorization. The university maintains full compliance with all regulations set forth by the law and will utilize E-Verify to assist in ensuring a legal workforce. An E-Verify case must be created no later than the third business day after the employee starts work for pay. All Form I-9 must be completed and received by the Office of Human Resources accordingly. 1 800 225 5588 21000 West Ten Mile Road Southfield, MI, 48075-1058 Instagram Streamline Icon: https://streamlinehq.com Facebook-f X-twitter Tiktok Linkedin Streamline Icon: https://streamlinehq.com Quick Links News Calendar Alumni Giving Faculty + Staff BannerWeb eHelp Library News Calendar Alumni Giving Faculty + Staff BannerWeb eHelp Library Admissions Apply Explore + Visit Academics Programs Course Catalog Financial Aid Tuition and Fees Apply Explore + Visit Academics Programs Course Catalog Financial Aid Tuition and Fees Student Life Housing Student Support Student Organizations Athletics Bookstore Library Housing Student Support Student Organizations Athletics Bookstore Library About Contact Us Campus Map Job Openings Research + Economic Development Office of the President Office of t